# DocAtlas documentation rules

When editing files under `doc-atlas/`:

- Use confidence tags: `[verified]`, `[likely]`, `[uncertain]`, `[planned]`
- Keep file paths accurate and copy-pasteable
- Update related docs when behavior changes

## File purposes

- `doc-atlas/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` — system design, components, data flow
- `doc-atlas/docs/ONBOARDING.md` — setup and first-day guide
- `doc-atlas/docs/RUNBOOK.md` — run, deploy, troubleshoot
- `doc-atlas/docs/GLOSSARY.md` — terms and abbreviations
- `doc-atlas/docs/JOURNEY-*.md` — traced user flows

## Drift

Before finishing doc edits, run `docatlas drift` or **`/docatlas`** (drift phase).
